 I cannot directly create an HTML page for you here, but I can certainly write you the code for such a page. Please note that this functionality requires accessing the user's local filesystem, which is not possible through standard web technologies due to security reasons. However, I can provide you with a simple HTML and JavaScript template for a button that, if run locally on your machine, will display an image from your file system. This example uses the File API.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Display Background Image</title>
    <style type="text/css">
        body {
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            overflow: hidden;
        }
        #image {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            object-fit: cover;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <button id="selectImageButton" onclick="displayBackgroundImage()">Select Background Image</button>
    <img id="image" src="" alt="Selected Background Image">

    <script type="text/javascript">
        function displayBackgroundImage() {
            document.getElementById('image').src = '';
            document.createElement('input');
            inputElement = document.createElement('input');
            inputElement.type = 'file';
            inputElement.accept = 'image/*';
            inputElement.onchange = function(event) {
                let reader = new FileReader();
                reader.readAsDataURL(event.target.files[0]);
                reader.onloadend = function() {
                    document.getElementById('image').src = reader.result;
                };
            };
            document.body.appendChild(inputElement);
            inputElement.click();
            document.body.removeChild(inputElement);
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This HTML page consists of a button that, when clicked, opens a file dialog allowing users to select an image file. Once selected, the image is displayed as the background of the page. Note that this code should be executed in a local environment

